  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14193754/assets/88e70630d7388f5f8acfe8f6ad6e0f1f254f9644f6035b51060bd44570c4902c.png)\n\nWhat is the range of the function $g$ defined by the mapping diagram shown above?",
  "worked_solution": "The range of $g(x)$ consists of all the outputs that have a corresponding $x$-input.\n\nIn a mapping diagram, the range consists of all the outputs to which an arrow is drawn.\n\nTherefore, the range is the set $\\{-2,0,3,5\\}.$",
